WEBVTT

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.300
Rikiishi!

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.390
Rikiishi-san, finish him quickly!

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.000
Rikiishi, you can do it!

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.880
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.880
You can do it, Bro Joe!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.230
Bro Joe!

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.880
Everyone in the audience, pay attention!

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.930
The match between Rikiishi Toru and Yabuki Joe is about to begin!

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.070
How exciting!

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.520
What do you think?

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.090
Well, let's see...

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.480
You could say Yabuki is ignorant of how horribly he's going to lose.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.750
That's right, that's right!

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.600
He's going to be all, "Crunch, crunchie, cruncho, into bits and pieces and—

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.790
Shut up about your "bits and pieces"!

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.540
Everyone, silence!

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.530
Silence, please!

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:29.500
Now, we would like to go through a few formalities before the match begins.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.520
First, the warden will be in charge of the gong and scorekeeping.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.430
As for the referee,

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:44.300
I believe the former boxer and future boxing instructor for this prison,

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.470
Tange Danpei-shi, should perform the task.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.500
W-Wait, Miss!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.800
I can't! I can't do that!

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.520
Why not?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.260
I'm busy enough just looking after Joe.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:01.490
P-Plus, if I were the referee, my judgments might be biased toward Joe.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.670
That would make this a pointless match.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.280
It'd be a mess!

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:10.500
Please, pick someone else to be the referee, Miss!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.780
How troubling.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.100
Even if you ask for someone else—

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.490
Well, Yohko-san, I was in the boxing club in high school.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.180
If it's all right, I can referee.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.290
I see.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.600
Please do.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.650
Now, before the match—

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.810
Who's that idiot!?

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.700
Who the heck is he!?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.070
Hurry it up!

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.680
What're you doing!?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.240
Rikiishi Toru.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.030
He's the first real obstacle I've ever faced.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.410
Now it's finally the time to take him on.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.360
I'm fired up to pummel you.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.480
Have you forgotten, Yabuki Joe?

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.540
I declared I'd knock you out in just one minute.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.670
You'll go down for good within one minute after the starting gong.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.270
Old man.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.070
Will Joe be okay?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.390
Don't worry, Nishi-kun.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.810
This isn't the same Joe as one week ago.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.010
I know that.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.760
He's got the punch for the Sake of Tomorrow you gave him, right?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.960
Well, yeah.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.090
Joe mastered it by fighting a group of inmates—

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.020
Fighting inmates?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.180
Yeah.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.770
Joe had a bunch of the inmates chase him,

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.470
and he stopped them one by one, using them as practice.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.590
I see. As expected of my disciple.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.240
Wait a minute...

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.960
Did Rikiishi see that!?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.410
He saw it.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.640
On top of analyzing Joe's punches,

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:20.840
Rikiishi did special training specifically for this match!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:48.650
If... If that's true, then this match is going to be horrific!

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.020
I-I have to do something!

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:50.860
I have to!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.290
Referee, before we start, we need to have a little chat!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.250
That's a problem. It'll interfere with the match.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:00.940
Sorry.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.760
This match is with amateur rules—three rounds, right?

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.040
Of course.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:11.260
And if someone is knocked down three times in one round, it'll be considered a TKO.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.770
It's that! I have a suggestion about that rule!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.030
Which is?

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.150
Instead of just three, no matter how many hundreds of times they go down,

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.280
you should let the boxers keep fighting until one surrenders!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.780
What?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.470
That rule was made for the safety of the boxers.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:34.330
It's an international rule.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.980
I know that, of course,

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.480
but isn't this match against the rules in the first place?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.570
Look at him.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:46.820
No matter how you look at it, he's a lightweight boxer.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.860
Joe, on the other hand, isn't even a bantamweight boxer.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.860
How do the rules allow boxers with this great a weight difference to fight?

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:57.770
Hey!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.810
Th-Then what should we...?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:06.820
Well, if we're overlooking that, you should allow my request, too!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:07.700
You're asking too much!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:11.320
If Yabuki-kun were to be killed because of that, what would we do?

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.530
What, you bastard!?

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.780
You saying Rikiishi can kill me!?

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.540
No, I didn't say anything like that...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.770
You bum referee...

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.540
Get out of my sight before I kill you!

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.680
B-But for this match, that's just—

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.710
Hey.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:29.550
Yes?

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.430
Let's go with their knockdown rule.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.560
You'll let us do it? Thanks!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:47.070
He thinks Joe can take me down more than three times with the secret punch he taught him?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.070
This old man!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.420
Well said!

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.040
I feel sorry for Joe!

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.940
Shut up, you bastards!

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:05.360
I'd normally come down and beat the crap out of you,

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:10.550
but I'm in a good mood, since I figured out that the old man thinks I'm a prodigy.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.480
And I didn't know, old man,

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:18.560
that the punch you gave me had enough power to take people down infinitely.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.690
Don't be so naïve.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:23.560
You're the one who's going to take a lot of downs, Joe.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.610
Wh-What?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.280
Joe's going to go down?

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.110
What do you mean!?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:30.940
Listen, Joe.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:37.050
That special punch requires endless blood and countless downs.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.830
You'll need to sacrifice some downs.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.910
Sacrifice?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:46.080
You mean Rikiishi has to beat me up for that punch to work!?

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.570
Don't joke with me!

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.590
My punch isn't that weak!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.630
You don't understand that punch.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.630
Pitiful, Joe.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.210
You'll lose.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.200
Lose?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.180
I don't understand!

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:07.190
Rikiishi was able to take down bulls!

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:09.690
Bulls?

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.490
Oh, no! Joe, open your mouth!

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.320
Your mouthpiece!

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:19.320
Go!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.930
Yahoo!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:37.900
Cool!

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.260
How's that for Rikiishi's power!?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.280
1!

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.350
2!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.480
3!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.160
Don't think badly of me.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.850
I did say I'd finish this in a minute.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.550
4!

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:50.150
5!

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.600
6!

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.030
Thanks to the old man's crazy talk,

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.110
7!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.150
look what's happened.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.240
8!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.360
9!

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.030
Shut up!

00:09:59.030 --> 00:09:59.890
He got up!

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.730
Go, Bro Joe!

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.080
Fight!

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:07.540
Your knees are already wobbling.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:17.900
He did it!

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.190
Bro Joe!

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:21.620
What's wrong?

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.510
Bro!

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.140
<i>Rikiishi-san!</i>

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:27.350
It's not even been a minute, you've still got 40 seconds! 40 seconds!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.560
Take your time! Take your time!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.390
Don't rush things over there, either.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:35.030
We still have to see if he'll stand up.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:35.970
4!

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:37.080
5!

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.030
6!

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.400
He did it!

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.110
He stood up!

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.170
Rikiishi-san, only 35 seconds!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.370
Bro Joe, you can do it!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.200
Hey, Yabuki Joe! It doesn't matter how many times you get up!

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.340
It's impossible!

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:06.710
Shut up, you guys.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.390
Don't make me laugh.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.310
Fight!

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.810
I won't let you take me down again!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:20.850
Joe, I didn't get to tell you why you'd lose.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:25.140
Being in the ring as a boxer means you're on the verge by yourself.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:30.640
You need to listen to the cries of your body!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:34.130
The fate of your tomorrow rests on this, your first match.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.770
Like a cold-hearted demon, I'll watch and not throw in the towel.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.550
I'm watching carefully!

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.770
1!

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.260
2!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.020
3!

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.580
I... I can't.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:49.690
4!

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.390
5!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.050
As expected of a former pro,

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:55.340
he doesn't show any openings.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:01.110
First, I really have to...

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.560
survive for more than a minute

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:07.090
and make him eat his words.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.110
He stood up again.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:15.110
<i>Fight!{bb= there's a bg voice, "mata tatta zo" "He stood up again"}</i>

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.880
Rikiishi-san! O-Only 15 seconds!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.880
Hey, what's wrong? Only 14 seconds now!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.890
Damn it...

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.560
Over here, over here! Yahoo!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.730
Over here, over here! 10 seconds!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:40.730
Over here, over here, idiot!

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.400
Wh-What's he doing?

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.220
All right, that's the way!

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:48.170
Joe, run! Keep running!

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:52.700
No matter what, don't let Rikiishi have his way!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.460
Rikiishi-san, only 6 seconds!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.460
Look, what can you do in 6 seconds?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.500
All right.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.300
You're trying to make your way here swiftly, eh?

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.550
I'm not letting you get away again.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.660
I said I won't let you get away.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.110
Wh-What's wrong?

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.530
I'm running so much, but he catches up so easily.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.820
This is called footwork.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.330
Bastard, get ready.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:48.930
He did it!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:52.390
That's exactly one minute! All right, way to go, Rikiishi-san!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.780
1!

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.400
2!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.980
3!

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.640
4!

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.200
5!

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.150
6!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:06.670
Joe!

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.430
Get up, Joe!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.920
Hey, what's wrong, Joe!?

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.860
Stand!

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.720
Stand up, Joe!

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:20.880
3!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.210
4!

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.720
5!

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.920
6!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.470
That's exactly one minute!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.430
Just like he promised!

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.710
D-Don't kid around with me, a KO?

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:49.090
I won't stay down for 10 seconds.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.760
8!

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:52.900
9!

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:53.370
10—

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.340
Stop the count!

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.270
It's been over a minute.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.420
Rikiishi-san, what'll you do now?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:16.950
Your declaration was a lie, you fake Cassius Clay!

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.760
What are you standing around for?

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.440
Come and get me!

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.020
He's invincible...

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.270
I, Rikiishi Toru, will make up for this

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:29.990
by beating him to death, Miss!

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.740
Remember this:

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.740
Yabuki Joe isn't just some sandbag!

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:38.660
Fight!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.460
He's got arms and legs!

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:50.720
Rikiishi-san!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.110
Joe, don't!

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:56.560
You can't go after him!

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.680
If you do, you'll lose!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.560
Idiot, Joe! Stop!

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:10.150
Damn it...

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:31.580
S-Stop!

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.750
Stop! Round One's over!

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.270
Damn, already?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.480
Joe, can you hear me?

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:48.100
This is good. That's the way to do it.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.940
Old man, you're cruel, too.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.610
About what?

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:58.740
You shouldn't say that to someone who's doing his best!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.140
Don't give me that bullshit!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.620
I'm Joe's second!

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:09.130
What Joe needs right now is some human compassion!

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.290
You're naïve, Nishi-kun.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.180
The fighting ring doesn't need people like that.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:15.910
Fighting machines are what's needed.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:18.380
In other words, ones who will fight to the end.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.600
It only needs a heartless machine.

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:24.060
Boring sympathy just gets in the way.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.140
Hey, get a hold of yourself, Joe.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.110
Hey!

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.090
Tarou, water, water!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.920
Here, here, take it. Move your mouth.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.840
Joe. Hang in there.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.840
Use the water to revive!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:50.100
J-Just a little more, and I would've had Rikiishi.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.550
You got in the way.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:57.050
Joe, you don't understand anything yet.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:02.170
Do you think you can still get past Rikiishi with those jabs and straights?

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:03.800
You'll just die a waste.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.850
If you think you've got a chance,

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:10.200
you need to take more downs.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:16.760
The path to victory starts opening when you're at the bottom.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:17.860
That is,

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.220
if you're still conscious and willing to fight.

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:39.060
Joe!

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:42.700
What're you doing? The gong hasn't rung yet.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:44.180
Move.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:47.730
Bro Joe!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:58.710
That's the sixth down!

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:07.250
Now that I don't have to finish you in a minute, I don't need to rush this match.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.180
Damn it...

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:57.210
Bring it.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:22.490
<i>Whip him harder!</i>

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.610
<i>Bro Joe!</i>

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:24.570
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.010
<i>Bro Joe!</i>

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:30.660
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:57.160
Wait.

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:02.040
Where do you think you're going?

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:07.920
Don't try to walk away... from this fire you started.

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.790
Eh, Miss?

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.380
Keep those pretty eyes open,

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:21.430
and watch to the very end.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:22.000
Got it?

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.690
Miss, when I know your pretty eyes are set on me,

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:30.000
I can bring out the power in my punches.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.970
Right, Bro Rikiishi?

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:34.970
Damn it...

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.980
Now, come at me, Rikiishi!

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:40.410
What's wrong?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:41.980
Hurry and get some!

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:46.450
O-Old man, h-he's done for!

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.830
At this rate, Joe's gonna die!

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:50.530
Towel! Throw in the towel!

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.240
I can't.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:53.240
Wh-Why?

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:57.140
If you throw in the towel, I'll kill you!

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:11.760
Miss, the time's come to end this tragedy.

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:05.650
There it is!

00:24:40.430 --> 00:24:47.180
The cross counter Joe finally brought out sank Rikiishi Toru.

00:24:47.970 --> 00:24:55.270
After countless downs and ups, Joe's guts finally bring victory!

00:24:55.270 --> 00:24:56.880
I was touched.

00:24:56.880 --> 00:24:58.420
I cried.

00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:02.730
My tomorrow with Joe is appearing before my eyes!

00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:06.360
Now, tomorrow's Joe...

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:07.950
Which way is tomorrow?
